Closing Statement

STIC explores a simple but fundamental idea:

System correctness emerges deterministically from structure — without requiring cloud infrastructure, centralized validation, or execution environments as a prerequisite.

Infrastructure may enable systems to run.
It does not determine whether they are correct.

It is released to encourage:

• independent validation
• real-world testing
• safe experimentation

STIC is offered as a minimal, verifiable reference implementation of that possibility.
